From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:38:39 -0400
Subject: ui: Arc parity round 5 -- the bar on the page, the Space title,
 downloads

The operator's side-by-side with Arc on beta 1 (docs/ARC-ROUND2.md, round
5). The address row sits directly on the content card and takes the page's
theme colour when it suits the colour scheme (SteddingWindowBackground and
a PageThemeColorController on the active tab); the active Space's icon and
name head the tab list with its pinned run and the Clear line beneath, then
"+ New Tab"; a per-Space pin now survives every relaunch (the incremental
session write and the startup rebuild share SpaceModel::SessionExtraDataForTab);
tab rows get quiet hover and active pills and the favicon column is the icon's
width; Space chips are bare 16 px emoji; a lone essential spans the row; the
sidebar edge drags on a 12 DIP handle; a two-finger swipe across the sidebar
changes Space; downloads live at the sidebar's bottom-left with the bubble
above them; Cmd-S toggles the sidebar (Save Page is Shift-Cmd-S); Cmd-T
classifies typed text the way the address bar does and lists the omnibox
providers' suggestions under the open tabs.

The visual audit of 2026-09-04 (docs/ARC-ROUND2.md, "Round 5 audit") adds:
the Space name pill is placed in the sidebar's coordinates (the switcher now
lives in the bottom row), every vertical tab's hover card opens beside the
sidebar (a pinned tab's used to open below its card, over the Space title),
and the settings hint names Cmd-S, the key that collapses the sidebar.

Why: every item is something a switcher from Arc noticed in the first day.

Removable when: never; this is product behaviour.
